# 3. CF-02 — ELIMINATE SYNTHETIC CROSS-SOURCE CONSENSUS

## Critical defect

The latest hostile audit found that `CrossValidator.ts` still creates a second `candidateValues` entry when only one source actually produced the metric.

This creates false consensus.

For example:

```text
Source A actually produced revenue = X
Source B produced nothing

Current system:
candidateValues = [
    Source A -> X,
    Source B -> X
]

Result:
EXACT_CONSENSUS
```

This is invalid.

## Required fix

`candidateValues` must contain **only independently observed/extracted values**.

If one source produced a fact:

```text
candidateValues = [
    Source A -> X
]
```

That is one-source evidence.

It must NOT become:

```text
Source B -> X
```

unless Source B independently produced X.

### Hard requirement

Delete the synthetic candidate-generation path.

Search for logic equivalent to:

```text
candidateValues.push(...)
```

or any fallback/copy/normalization logic that creates a source observation without an actual extraction event.

Remove or redesign it.

